[231.68987, "i", "cat > /home/user/firewall/FIX_SUMMARY.txt << 'EOF'\nFIREWALL FIX SUMMARY\n====================\n\nPROBLEM:\nTraffic from ML inference service (10.200.0.0/16) could not reach model registry (10.100.0.42:5000)\n\nROOT CAUSES:\n1. Rule was in wrong chain (INPUT instead of FORWARD)\n   - Gateway forwards traffic between networks, which uses FORWARD chain\n   - INPUT chain only handles traffic destined TO the gateway itself\n\n2. Explicit DROP rules were blocking the traffic\n   - Lines blocking all 10.200.0.0/16 -> 10.100.0.0/16 traffic\n   - These came BEFORE the general ACCEPT rules, so they took precedence\n\nFIXES APPLIED:\n1. Moved port 5000 ACCEPT rule from INPUT chain to FORWARD chain\n2. Removed the DROP rules that were blocking inter-network traffic\n3. Kept and enhanced bidirectional forwarding rules (eth1 <-> eth2)\n4. Made destination more specific (10.100.0.42) for the registry rule\n\nRESULT:\nInference service traffic can now reach the model registry on port 5000\nEOF\n"]
